    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ \\overline{y}_{i} $. is the sample mean for factor i and $ \\overline{y} $. is the overall sample mean. As we will see shortly, these sums of squares have degrees of freedom N - 1 and $ N(n-1) $, respectively. The test for a significant treatment effect (at least one $ \\tau_{i} \\neq 0 $) is the F-ratio statistic",
